WEBVTT

00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:17,840
How much does my attitude affect my cancer really? I think that's how much does my cancer?

00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:26,910
How much does my attitude really affect my health or my cancer? Well, I think it affects

00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:32,990
your body a lot. If you're talking about just a good attitude, bad attitude, happy,

00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:40,590
crabby, you know, I think there's a lot of biblical reference to be grateful. And you know,

00:00:41,470 --> 00:00:47,790
the, you know, there's a lot of new agey kind of positive mental attitude stuff. But really,

00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:54,190
you could argue that it is growing, typically as well. I wouldn't say that there's any

00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:59,630
biblical stance that if you just have a good attitude, everything's going to be good. But

00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:04,670
it does tell us, typically, that we're supposed to be grateful and thankful for everything.

00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:08,110
The fruits of the spirit, our love, joy, peace, patience, goodness, kindness,

00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:18,830
gratefulness, self-control. These are all outward acts. The fruit of the spirit is the fruit that

00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:27,790
comes from a tree that's grounded in God. So if we're grounded in our Father, in our Heavenly Father,

00:01:27,790 --> 00:01:35,630
then we're going to bear good fruit. So I guess I would say that our attitude is the fruit

00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:41,710
of what we're grounded in. So if I am, you know, I have a day that I'm crabby and angry,

00:01:42,510 --> 00:01:50,830
which I have a lot of days like that. I have to look at what am I holding on to? Is it the situate?

00:01:50,830 --> 00:01:58,910
Is it my positive situation that's going to make me happy? Or am I grounded in my relationship with

00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:05,390
Jesus Christ through Jesus Christ to my Heavenly Father that's going to give me joy? That's going to

00:02:05,390 --> 00:02:12,350
bear the fruit that we call our attitude. You know, when I have a bad attitude, I got to look at

00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:21,870
where where my groundedness is. Am I really grafted into the tree of our Heavenly Father?

00:02:22,830 --> 00:02:27,070
That's the question I have to ask myself. When we need to all be introspective enough,

00:02:27,070 --> 00:02:33,390
and we need to all have close enough friends and in loved ones in our life that can

00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:41,310
slap us a little bit and we need to all not take offense, but we do have some wood in our life that

00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:50,030
loves us enough to slap us a little bit to remind us of where we're supposed to be grafted into

00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:57,630
and grounded into and so that we will produce the fruit of the spirit in our lives.

00:02:59,310 --> 00:03:05,310
And that's what accountability is and that's what, you know, spiritual maturity is,

00:03:05,950 --> 00:03:13,710
is, you know, said many times, spiritual maturity isn't not sitting. It's that we are more quickly

00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:23,870
convicted of our sin in our bad attitude and more quickly repent of that bad attitude

00:03:24,430 --> 00:03:34,110
and and bring and come back into submission to our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ. So

00:03:34,830 --> 00:03:45,070
the more I, the longer I take to come back into submission to my to my Lord is a sign of

00:03:45,070 --> 00:03:50,990
less maturity. As I mature, doesn't mean I'm not going to screw up more and have a bad attitude

00:03:50,990 --> 00:04:03,950
and be frammy. It means that I'll be convicted more quickly and be able to come back into submission.

